\begin{warning}{Alternative Hypotheses}
\textbf{Some Predictors Could Have Opposite Effects:}

\textbf{1. Road Density - Ambiguous:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Positive:} More roads $\rightarrow$ More spread (pathogen transport)
    \item \textbf{Negative:} More roads $\rightarrow$ Better access $\rightarrow$ Faster veterinary response $\rightarrow$ Better control
    \item \textbf{Empirical question:} Which effect dominates?
\end{itemize}

\textbf{2. GDP - Ambiguous:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Negative:} Higher GDP $\rightarrow$ Better control capacity
    \item \textbf{Positive:} Higher GDP $\rightarrow$ More intensive farming $\rightarrow$ Higher density $\rightarrow$ More transmission
    \item \textbf{Likely:} Net negative (control capacity outweighs intensification)
\end{itemize}

\textbf{3. Tree Cover - Context-Dependent:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Positive (ASF):} Forest $\rightarrow$ Wild boar $\rightarrow$ Spillover
    \item \textbf{Negative (other diseases):} Forest $\rightarrow$ Barrier to movement $\rightarrow$ Reduced spread
    \item \textbf{Disease-specific:} Depends on wildlife reservoir
\end{itemize}

These ambiguities make the analysis interesting. Results will adjudicate between competing hypotheses.
\end{warning}

